0,Kurumba languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kurumba_languages,"Kurumba (also known as Kuruba in Karnataka and Kuruma in Kerala, IPA: [kuru (m)bɐ, kurumɐ]), refers to a group of languages within the Southern Dravidian branch of the Dravidian language family [3][4] These languages are spoken by the Kurumba communities, who inhabit Nilgiri Hills, in Tamil Nadu and nearby areas including of Coimbatore, Pudukottai etc. [5] The cultural identity of the ...","Kurumba, Mullu",Dravidian
1,Mullu Kurumba language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mullu_Kurumba_language,Mullu Kurumba (IPA: [muɭːu kurum (b)ɐ]) is a Southern Dravidian language closely related to Malayalam.,"Kurumba, Mullu",Dravidian
2,Kurumba languages — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/kurumba_languages,"The Kurumba languages, a cluster of closely related Southern Dravidian varieties spoken by tribal communities in southern India, are often informally grouped by areal influences and dialectal divergences rather than strict genetic subgroups, with some like Betta and Jenu showing Kannada-like features, Mullu aligning closely with Irula through ...","Kurumba, Mullu",Dravidian
