5,Mullu kurumba Tribe Dance - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z1WTBD2rCIg,"Enjoy the videos and music you love, upload original content, and share it all with friends, family, and the world on YouTube.","Kurumba, Mullu",Dravidian
6,Kurumba - DOBES,https://dobes.mpi.nl/projects/kurumba/,"The 'Kurumba' groups we document are scattered on the borders of the three southern states and identified under a variety of names: Alu Kurumbas and Jenu Kurumbas in Tamil Nadu, Cholanaikkas, Kattunaikkas and Mullu Kurumbas in Kerala, Jenu Kurubas in Karnataka.","Kurumba, Mullu",Dravidian
7,"Kurumbagounder | Kuruman Indigenous Community, Culture & History",https://www.kurumbagounder.org/,"Kurumbagounder is a cultural and awareness platform dedicated to documenting the history, culture, voices, and rights of the Kuruman (Kurumba) indigenous community of South India. The website highlights ancestral heritage, forest livelihoods, legal recognition, and contemporary challenges faced by the Kuruman people.","Kurumba, Mullu",Dravidian
8,People & Culture - DOBES,https://dobes.mpi.nl/projects/kurumba/people/,"Mullu Kurumbas The Mullu Kurumbas live in a few places in the forest areas of the Wayanad district of Kerala. They are well known for their hunting and bird catching traditions though they predominantly practice agriculture in the Vayals of the Wayanad. Today, many of them are pretty well educated and have jobs involving them in the modern economy as well. Compared to the other Kurumba groups ...","Kurumba, Mullu",Dravidian
9,National Tribal Virtual Art & Culture Portal (ADI KALAKAR Portal),https://adikalakar.tribal.gov.in/ViewDashDetails.aspx?id=MTUy,"Vattakali is an old musical dance form of the Kurumba tribes. The work vattam means circle, kali means dance or game or play and vattakali means a circular dance.Vatakali and Kolkali are some of the traditional dance forms of Mullu Kurumbas where Vatakali is performed during the marriage rituals and Kolkali is performed during temple rituals.","Kurumba, Mullu",Dravidian
